vendor headers follow real identifier and namespace tokens: true
longer identifiers comments and literals cannot inject vendor headers: true
qualified tokens match across spaces and comments: true
a commented include cannot suppress a required header: true
direct compiler preparation is idempotent: true
builtin dependencies retain declaration order: true
builtin decoys share the vendor token scan: true
single compiler receives the sanitized emitted symbol once: true
single compile returns the original compiler-owned object: true
static parameters retain binding order: true
batch compiles one source and shares compiler ownership: true
batch artifact uses the trimmed common prefix: true
batch metadata preserves routine order: true
batch source preserves procedure order: true
compiler failure crosses the driver without replacing its identity: true
failure context appends the exact effective option vector: true
